  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I is shown to interact with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a key component of the microtubule network in cells. This protein is a target of two distinct molecular structures, both of which are implicated in the regulation of microtubule dynamics. These structures are specifically targeted by BT-474, a cell line that is known to be sensitive to microtubule-targeting agents. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Sasanquasaponin I may exert its effects on BT-474, possibly through the modulation of microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a well-documented target of microtubule inhibitors. The presence of multiple molecular targets that are functionally related to microtubule dynamics supports the hypothesis that Sasanquasaponin I may act through a microtubule-inhibiting mechanism in BT-474 cells. The integration of these findings provides a plausible pathway for the observed interaction, although further experimental validation is required to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic potential.",
